## 9.1 Docker Strategy

### Current Problems
1. ChromeDriver version must match installed Chrome exactly
2. `webdriver-manager` downloads binaries at runtime (fails in air-gapped environments)
3. No official Selenium Python Docker image with browser included
4. OpenCV native dependencies are heavy

### Playwright Docker Solution

```dockerfile
# Dockerfile.playwright
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/playwright/python:v1.49.0-noble

WORKDIR /app

# Install Python dependencies
COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

# Install Playwright browsers (already included in base image, 
# but this ensures version match with pip package)
RUN playwright install --with-deps chromium

# Copy application
COPY . .

# Expose ports
EXPOSE 8001

# Health check
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=10s --retries=3 \
    CMD curl -f http://localhost:8001/api/health || exit 1

# Run
CMD ["uvicorn", "backend.main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8001"]
```

### Docker Compose

```yaml
# docker-compose.yml
version: '3.8'

services:
  qa-agent:
    build:
      context: .
      dockerfile: Dockerfile.playwright
    ports:
      - "8001:8001"
    environment:
      - BROWSER_ENGINE=playwright
      - GROQ_API_KEY=${GROQ_API_KEY}
      - PINECONE_API_KEY=${PINECONE_API_KEY}
      - PINECONE_INDEX_NAME=${PINECONE_INDEX_NAME}
      - SUPABASE_URL=${SUPABASE_URL}
      - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=${SUPABASE_ANON_KEY}
      - LLM_PROVIDER=groq
    volumes:
      - test-results:/app/test_results
      - project-data:/app/backend/data/projects
    deploy:
      resources:
        limits:
          memory: 4G
          cpus: '2'
    restart: unless-stopped

  # Optional: Redis for task queue (future)
  # redis:
  #   image: redis:7-alpine
  #   ports:
  #     - "6379:6379"

volumes:
  test-results:
  project-data:
```

### Why Playwright Containers Are Easier

| Concern | Selenium Docker | Playwright Docker |
|---------|----------------|-------------------|
| **Base image** | Custom: install Chrome + ChromeDriver + match versions | Official: `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright/python` |
| **Browser install** | Manual apt-get + version pinning | `playwright install --with-deps` |
| **Version sync** | Must manually match Chrome ↔ ChromeDriver | Auto-synced by Playwright package version |
| **Image freshness** | Manual updates, version drift | Microsoft maintains official images |
| **Sandbox issues** | `--no-sandbox` + `--disable-dev-shm-usage` flags needed | Same flags, but better documented |
| **Multi-browser** | Separate images for Firefox, Edge | Single image supports Chromium, Firefox, WebKit |
| **Size** | ~1.2GB | ~1.4GB (includes all browsers) or ~900MB (Chromium only) |
| **ARM support** | Limited | Full ARM64 support |

## 9.2 Kubernetes Architecture

```yaml
# k8s/deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: qa-agent
spec:
  replicas: 2
  strategy:
    type: RollingUpdate
    rollingUpdate:
      maxSurge: 1
      maxUnavailable: 0
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: qa-agent
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: qa-agent
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: qa-agent
          image: qa-agent:latest
          ports:
            - containerPort: 8001
          resources:
            requests:
              memory: "2Gi"
              cpu: "1"
            limits:
              memory: "4Gi"
              cpu: "2"
          env:
            - name: BROWSER_ENGINE
              value: "playwright"
            - name: BROWSER_POOL_MAX
              value: "3"
          volumeMounts:
            - name: test-results
              mountPath: /app/test_results
            - name: shm
              mountPath: /dev/shm
          livenessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /api/health
              port: 8001
            initialDelaySeconds: 30
            periodSeconds: 30
          readinessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /api/health
              port: 8001
            initialDelaySeconds: 10
            periodSeconds: 10
      volumes:
        - name: test-results
          persistentVolumeClaim:
            claimName: test-results-pvc
        - name: shm
          emptyDir:
            medium: Memory
            sizeLimit: 2Gi
```

## 9.3 Blue-Green Migration Strategy

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph "Phase 1: Green (Current)"
        G1[Selenium Engine] --> G2[Production Traffic 100%]
    end
    
    subgraph "Phase 2: Canary"
        B1[Playwright Engine] --> B2[10% Traffic]
        G1 --> G3[90% Traffic]
    end
    
    subgraph "Phase 3: Split"
        B1b[Playwright Engine] --> B3[50% Traffic]
        G1b[Selenium Engine] --> G4[50% Traffic]
    end
    
    subgraph "Phase 4: Blue (Target)"
        B1c[Playwright Engine] --> B4[100% Traffic]
        G1c[Selenium Standby] --> G5[0% - Rollback Ready]
    end
```

**Feature flag implementation**:
```python
# backend/core/config.py
class Settings:
    # ... existing settings ...
    BROWSER_ENGINE = os.getenv("BROWSER_ENGINE", "selenium")  # "selenium" | "playwright" | "auto"
    PLAYWRIGHT_ROLLOUT_PERCENT = int(os.getenv("PLAYWRIGHT_ROLLOUT_PERCENT", "0"))
```

## 9.4 CI/CD Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Push to main] --> B[Build Docker Image]
    B --> C[Install Playwright Browsers]
    C --> D[Run Unit Tests]
    D --> E[Run Integration Tests with Playwright]
    E --> F{Tests Pass?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Push to Registry]
    F -->|No| H[Block Deployment]
    G --> I[Deploy to Staging]
    I --> J[Smoke Tests]
    J --> K{Smoke Pass?}
    K -->|Yes| L[Deploy to Production]
    K -->|No| M[Rollback]
```

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml (key section)
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    container:
      image: mcr.microsoft.com/playwright/python:v1.49.0-noble
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -r requirements.txt
      - run: playwright install --with-deps chromium
      - run: python -m pytest tests/ -v
      - run: python -m pytest tests/integration/ -v --browser chromium
```
